
⚙️ DFDL Parsing & Serialization (Automatic vs Manual)

Type	Control	Description	Example

Automatic	By Node	Input/Output nodes (MQInput, FileInput, HTTPInput, MQOutput, etc.) khud parsing & serialization handle karte hain.	MQInput → DFDL parser → Message Tree <br> MQOutput → Message Tree → Bitstream
Manual	By Code	ESQL ya JavaCompute node me programmer manually parsing / serialization karta hai.	CREATE ... PARSE() → Bytes → Tree <br> ASBITSTREAM() → Tree → Bytes



---

🔹 Input / Output Node (Automatic)

Node Type	Operation	Action

Input Node	Parsing	Raw bitstream ko schema ke hisaab se parse karke Message Tree banata hai
Output Node	Serialization	Message Tree ko wapas bitstream (bytes) me convert karta hai


✅ Example:
MQInput node par binary data aaya → DFDL selected → Automatically parsed into tree
MQOutput node → Same schema → Automatically serialized into bytes


---

🔹 ESQL / API (Manual)

ESQL Statement	Direction	Meaning

CREATE ... PARSE(BLOB ... CCSID ENCODING)	Bytes → Tree	Manually parse bytes into Message Tree
ASBITSTREAM(OutputRoot ... ENCODING CCSID)	Tree → Bytes	Manually serialize tree into bitstream (for logs, DB, etc.)



---

⚖️ Difference (1-Line Summary)

Automatic (Node-Based)	Manual (Code-Based)

Flow node khud handle karta hai	Developer explicitly control leta hai
Less control, faster integration	Full control, custom logic possible



---

🧩 Example Scenario

Step	Description

1️⃣	MQInput node → Automatic Parsing
2️⃣	ESQL (ASBITSTREAM) → Manual Serialization for logging
3️⃣	MQOutput node → Automatic Serialization



---

👉 Summary Line:

> Automatic = Node sambhalta hai 💡
Manual = Developer handle karta hai (for custom parse/serialize) 🧠

